# Cursor  
#  Cursor is an AI-powered code editor.`.cursorignore` specifies files/directories to 
#  exclude from AI features like autocomplete and code analysis. Recommended for sensitive data
#  refer to https://docs.cursor.com/context/ignore-files
.cursorignore
.cursorindexingignore
*.jpg
*.mp4
/configs
/recorded_videos

# No image under data/ is versioned, in any format, anywhere, with no
# exceptions. Captures are fetched or copied in and placed under
# data/; overlays, plots and conversions then appear locally when a
# pipeline runs. What stays in git is the trail that makes a result
# traceable: the records the scripts write, the result tables, the region
# definitions and the instructions to reproduce them.
#
# One rule over the whole tree rather than one per folder, so a new
# folder under data/ inherits it instead of silently committing images
# beside ignored siblings. Extensions mirror .gitattributes, which routes
# the same set to LFS, and are case sensitive, so both spellings appear
# where the camera and the tooling disagree.
data/**/*.NEF
data/**/*.nef
data/**/*.DNG
data/**/*.dng
data/**/*.CR2
data/**/*.cr2
data/**/*.ARW
data/**/*.arw
data/**/*.png
data/**/*.PNG
data/**/*.jpg
data/**/*.JPG
data/**/*.jpeg
data/**/*.JPEG
data/**/*.tif
data/**/*.TIF
data/**/*.tiff
data/**/*.TIFF
data/**/*.bmp
data/**/*.BMP
data/**/*.webp
data/**/*.WEBP
data/**/*.gif

# Per-image label files are derived and are not versioned either. A YOLO .txt
# is a projection of the annotation it was exported from, so it can be
# regenerated, while the export cannot be recovered from it: the LabelMe json
# under a dataset's source/ holds polygons and class names, the .txt holds
# four numbers and a class index. The json is the manual work and stays.
#
# Scoped to labels/ rather than the whole dataset so a classes.txt or a split
# definition at a dataset root is not swept up with them.
data/datasets/**/labels/**/*.txt

# Framework scratch written beside a dataset when it is first read.
data/**/*.cache

# The COCO source tree in full. It is downloaded rather than produced here,
# it is 20 GB, and it carries annotation json and split lists that the image
# and label rules above would not catch. Nothing in it is ours to version.
data/datasets/coco/

# Model weights. Every one is either downloaded from a pinned release URL or
# produced by a fine-tuning run here, so none of them is ours to version, and
# the five pre-trained files alone are about 2 GB. data/models/README.md lists
# each with its source and size.
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine
*.safetensors

# Validation and training output. Every run here is reproducible from
# sweep.json plus the weights and datasets, and one sweep writes 77 folders
# of plots, sample images and predictions.json. What belongs in git is the
# config that produced them, not the output.
/runs/
